  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "Achieving a 120,000× improvement in fusion yield from current 0.25 J/shot (D) to 30 kJ/shot (p-B11) net energy target",
      "Quantum magnetic field (QMF) effect must work as theorized to suppress bremsstrahlung losses sufficiently for p-B11 net energy",
      "Ion beam decelerator achieving 85% efficiency on the divergent, multi-species, ~10 ns DPF ion beam",
      "X-ray photoelectric converter achieving 80%+ efficiency in a 'never-before-built multilayered photoelectric vacuum tube'",
      "200 Hz repetition rate operation at 2.7 MA with monthly electrode replacement cadence",
      "Resolving the 22-year filament disruption yield plateau through better plasma compression and expanded capacitor bank (I⁴ scaling)",
      "Q_sci substantially above breakeven (≥2.5) to keep recirculating fraction commercially viable (~57%)"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "Tritium supply chain entirely eliminated — no tritium breeding blanket, no FLiBe/LiPb procurement, no lithium-6 enrichment (CAS27 Special Materials = $0)",
      "First wall/blanket eliminated — aneutronic fuel means no neutron-handling blanket structure (CAS22.01 = $0)",
      "External confinement magnets eliminated — self-pinch confinement requires no REBCO superconducting tape or external coils (CAS22.03 = $0)",
      "Turbine plant eliminated — direct energy conversion replaces thermal cycle (CAS23 = $0)",
      "Supplementary heating eliminated — no NBI or ECRH systems required (CAS22.04 = $0)"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "Direct Energy Converter (CAS22.09) — entirely novel dual-path device combining ion beam decelerator and x-ray photoelectric converter, with no library analogue",
      "Beryllium electrode supply at ~4,000 t/year fleet scale (10× current global production) with monthly replacement cadence",
      "Isotopically enriched B-11 decaborane fuel — currently $600/gram, hand-produced via single-source Russian isotopic purification + Czech synthesis",
      "Capacitor bank as primary capital item (CAS22.07) handling full 23 MW recirculating power per module at 200 Hz duty cycle",
      "C-11 radioactive exhaust management at 200 Hz commercial rep-rates (20-min half-life accumulation)"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "Yield plateau at 0.25 J/shot has been unresolved for over 20 years; reaching 30 kJ/shot net target requires 120,000× improvement combining four undemonstrated multiplicative factors",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Quantum magnetic field (QMF) bremsstrahlung suppression has no experimental confirmation in any device; without it, p-B11 net energy is energetically impossible under classical physics",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Neither the ion beam decelerator nor the x-ray photoelectric converter has a prototype, component test, or engineering design — and there is no thermal cycle fallback if DEC underperforms",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "DEC efficiency sensitivity is severe: η_dec < 0.65 drives net power negative (plant eliminated); η_dec = 0.75 roughly doubles LCOE vs 0.85 baseline",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "200 Hz repetition rate at 2.7 MA never demonstrated; best analogue (NX2 in Singapore) is 16 Hz at far lower currents for non-fusion applications",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "High recirculating fraction (82% at FOAK Q=1.72, 57% at NOAK Q=2.5) requires plant to produce 5-6× net electric output as gross fusion power, driving high specific capital",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Isotopic B-11 enrichment supply chain is single-sourced through Russia (purification) and Czech Republic (synthesis), creating geopolitical concentration risk",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "No independent verification of LPPFusion's >200 keV ion temperature or record plasma purity claims by any national lab, university, or peer institution",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Electrode erosion rate at 2.7 MA × 200 Hz is completely uncharacterized, making variable O&M cost (electrode replacement at monthly cadence) a significant unknown",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Filament disruption at high current limits yield growth — identified as current experimental blocker with no demonstrated solution",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Beryllium supply at fleet scale (~4,000 t/year, 10× current global production) requires processing lower-grade ores with toxicity handling requirements not quantified at scale",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "p-B11 fusion yield in a DPF has never been measured; 2024 Frontiers paper describes preparations only, not results",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Simultaneous high density (10²¹ cm⁻³) and high ion energy (>200 keV) has been demonstrated separately but not concurrently",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "C-11 radioactive byproduct management at 200 Hz commercial rep-rates is uncharacterized; even small per-pulse production accumulates significantly given 20-min half-life",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ]
  },
